{
	"//": "vs-kot: JSON has no comments, so the fork's edits to this file are listed here. Changed: the product identity (name*, applicationName, *DataFolderName, server*/tunnel* names, win32*, darwin*, linux*, urlProtocol), and licenseUrl, serverLicenseUrl and reportIssueUrl, which point at this repository instead of Microsoft's. Added: extensionsGallery (Open VSX). Added for the team: vsKotManagedSettings (locked settings), vsKotDefaultSettings (changeable defaults) and the team's extensions in builtInExtensions (Prettier, Auto Close Tag, Auto Rename Tag, ES7+ React snippets). The default for editor.quickSuggestions is the classic one: with upstream's newer default the editor drops a tab completion that takes longer than 750 ms. editor.suggest.selectionMode is whenQuickSuggestion: right after a trigger character such as a dot the suggestion list selects nothing, so tab completion may propose any member instead of having to continue the first list entry. Added for updates: vsKotVersion (our release number; raise it for every release, the tag is v plus this number), vsKotUpdatePublicKeys (the public halves of the keys a release may be signed with; the app installs nothing that is not signed with one of them, and the private half is with whoever publishes releases, see .vs-kot/sign-release.sh), updateUrl (where the app looks for latest.json, the file every release carries) and downloadUrl (the page people are sent to when the app cannot replace itself).",
